# Auto-push to GitHub

After finishing any code or config change in this repo:

1. Stage relevant files (`git add`). Never stage `.env.local` or secrets.
2. Commit with a short message that explains why.
3. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push -u origin HEAD`).

Do this at the end of every task, even if the user did not repeat "commit" or "push". A project hook also pushes when the agent turn stops; still push yourself so GitHub is up to date before the turn ends.
